# Next.js App Router

Source: PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules `rules/nextjs-app-router-cursorrules-prompt-file.mdc`, adapted to this TypeScript App Router app.

## Server Components by default

- Every new `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, and shared component is a Server Component.
- Add `"use client"` only for state, effects, event handlers, or browser APIs (file picker, clipboard, video controls).
- Keep the client boundary as small as possible. Do not mark a whole route client just to use one button.
- Fetch data in the Server Component or call FastAPI from a small client island. Do not add a new `useEffect` fetch when the server can pass the data in.

```tsx
// BAD — whole page is client because one control needs state
"use client";
export default function Page() { /* entire dashboard */ }

// GOOD — server page, client island for the control that needs the browser
export default function Page() {
  return <UploadDropzone />;
}
```

## App Router

- Routes live under `frontend/app/`. Special files: `layout.tsx`, `page.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`.
- Export `metadata` from server layouts/pages. Do not export `metadata` from a client component.
- Style with Tailwind. Use `next/image` for raster images. Read config from env vars, never hardcoded secrets.
- This UI is RTL Hebrew. New layout must keep `dir="rtl"` on the page shell.
